          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0003> having (RS*).\nLet <MATH_0004> be an object of\n<MATH_0005> over an affine scheme <MATH_0006> of finite type over <MATH_0007>.\nLet <MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009> be a finite type points such that\n(a) there are no specializations <MATH_0010> for <MATH_0011>, and\n(b) <MATH_0012> is not versal at <MATH_0013> for all <MATH_0014>. Then there exist morphisms\n<MATHSEG_0001>in <MATHSEG_0002> lying over <MATHSEG_0003>\nover <MATH_0015> such that\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> for each <MATH_0016> the morphism <MATH_0017> is a first order\nthickening,\n<STRUCT_0004> for each <MATH_0018> we have a short exact sequence\n<MATH_0019>\nwith <MATH_0020> for <MATH_0021>,\n<STRUCT_0005> for each <MATH_0022> there does <TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> exist a pair <MATH_0023>\nconsisting of an open neighbourhood <MATH_0024> of <MATH_0025>\nand a morphism <MATH_0026>\nsuch that the composition\n<MATHSEG_0004>restriction of <MATHSEG_0005>\nis the canonical morphism <MATH_0027>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007>",
          "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f94cdf922bfeae64c9d2c1619b9ffb55b9de7cfddcaabd44703d354d7d2c6e3",
