          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0003> having (RS*).\nLet <MATH_0004> be an object of <MATH_0005> over an affine scheme <MATH_0006>\nof finite type over <MATH_0007>. Let <MATH_0008> be a finite type point such that\n<MATH_0009> is not versal at <MATH_0010>. Then there exists a morphism <MATH_0011>\nof <MATH_0012> lying over <MATH_0013> satisfying\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> the morphism <MATH_0014> is a first order thickening,\n<STRUCT_0004> we have a short exact sequence\n<MATH_0015>\n<STRUCT_0005> there does <TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> exist a pair <MATH_0016>\nconsisting of an open neighbourhood <MATH_0017> of <MATH_0018>\nand a morphism <MATH_0019> such that the composition\n<MATHSEG_0001>restriction of <MATHSEG_0002>\nis the canonical morphism <MATH_0020>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007>",
          "source_text_hash": "sha256:b9ec5cb04a1ce8f46d6e9b6386d73aa046e7b1aa810c1d8e5f517158fa1ff07b",
          "unit_id": "inventory:artin:0G2J:lemma/0001"
        }
      }
